  "description": "Te Tai Tokerau is the northernmost Māori electorate. It covers the Northland region, Auckland’s North Shore and cuts through West Auckland suburbs. The seat is held by Mariameno Kapa-Kingi, who was first elected in 2023 as a member of Te Pāti Māori. Kapa-Kingi won with 10,428 votes and 26% of the party vote and is now running as the leader of Te Tai Tokerau Party, having fallen out with Te Pāti Māori leadership. \n\n",
